# Template for .env.admin - used ONLY by `npm run set-admin` (scripts/set-admin.ts).
# Copy to .env.admin (gitignored) and fill in the PRODUCTION database URL.
# The rest of the tooling (dev, tests, migrations) keeps using .env.local - the two
# files must never be swapped, so an accidental `npm test` or `db:push` can never
# reach production through this file.
#
# How to reach the production database safely: open an SSH tunnel to the VPS first,
#   ssh -N -L 15432:127.0.0.1:5432 root@164.138.216.72
# then point the URL at the tunnel (host 127.0.0.1, port 15432). Get the password
# from /srv/wheelylove/.env (POSTGRES_PASSWORD) on the VPS.
#
# Alternative without a tunnel: run the same command inside the app container on
# the VPS (see deploy/README.md).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://wheely:CHANGE_ME_PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:15432/wheelylove
